{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And Joseph remembered the dreams which he dreamed about them.</b> He remembered the dreams concerning them: in the dream of the sheaves all of them were bowing, and his sheaf arose and also stood erect — it did not fall after rising. Therefore he wanted all of them to come and report it, so that the matter of \"and also stood erect\" would be fulfilled in him. And this is by merit of his being a hint to the future redeemer, after the manner of יְרֵה וַיּוֹר (2 Kings 13:17), as it says: וְנִקְבְּצוּ בְּנֵי יְהוּדָה וּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל יַחְדָּיו וְשָׂמוּ לָהֶם רֹאשׁ אֶחָד (Hosea 2:2), and the matter of \"and also stood erect\" will be fulfilled in them, as it says: מַלְכוּ דִּי לְעָלְמִין לָא תִתְחַבַּל (Daniel 2:44)." "<b>You have come to see the nakedness of the land.</b> To see whether there is enough food for our land — and you have not come to buy, for it is not the custom of other arrivals that ten should come together making inquiry."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {0 "Sforno reads וְגַם נִצָּבָה (Gen. 37:7) as indicating permanence — the sheaf stood and never fell — and connects this typologically to the future redeemer and an eternal kingdom."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:19.949773377Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}